hria, and dysphagia (due to disruption of corticospinal and corticobulbar tracts).</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">2.&nbsp; **Stroke Evolution vs. Inadequate Antiplatelet Response:** The patient experienced a "stuttering" onset—initially presenting on 05/05, discharging after transient improvement, then worsening severely on 05/06. This pattern is classic for basilar branch disease or atherothrombotic pontine infarction.&nbsp;</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">3.&nbsp; **Vascular Cognitive Impairment (VCI):** Although initial consult noted "cognition intact," the subsequent formal OT assessment on 05/11 revealed clear deficits in attention, memory, and orientation. This could represent an acute post-stroke confusional state or vascular cognitive decline unmasked by the pontine event.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a"><br></font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">#### Recommended Evaluations &amp; Managements</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">*&nbsp; &nbsp;**Etiology &amp; Secondary Prevention Survey:** Since high flow velocity was noted in the left ECA and bilateral plaques exist, a strict cardiac and metabolic workup is necessary to differentiate between large artery atherosclerosis and a cardioembolic source.&nbsp;</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">*&nbsp; &nbsp;**Dysphagia Management:** While the patient tolerated an IDDSI Level 4 diet under ST supervision, she still has a delayed swallow reflex (3 seconds) and a delayed/decreased laryngeal elevation. A formal **Videofluoroscopic Swallow Study (VFSS)** or **Fiberoptic Endoscopic Evaluation of Swallowing (FEES)** is recommended before advancing to regular textures to minimize silent aspiration risk.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">*&nbsp; &nbsp;**Cognitive Intervention:** Formal OT cognitive rehabilitation should be integrated alongside motor training, given the deficits identified on 05/11.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a"><br></font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">#### Missing Information &amp; Discrepancies</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">1.&nbsp; **Etiology Reports:** The Brain MRI/MRA and Carotid Duplex reports are mentioned as completed, but specific details are missing: Is there an **EKG or 24-hour Holter monitoring report** to rule out paroxysmal Atrial Fibrillation? Is there a **Transthoracic/Transesophageal Echocardiogram (TTE/TEE)** report to evaluate for a cardiac source of emboli?&nbsp;</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">2.&nbsp; **Lab Data:** There is a complete lack of metabolic baseline data documented. We require **HbA1c, fasting glucose, and a complete lipid profile (LDL, HDL, TG)** to optimize her secondary stroke prevention.</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">3.&nbsp; **Physical Examination Contradictions:** In the physiatrist consult note on 05/07, the template states *"BADLs: independent"*, which directly contradicts the clinical picture of *mRS 5, bedrest, NG tube, and Foley insertion*. This appears to be a copy-paste error from the premorbid section and needs correction to *"BADLs: totally dependent"*.&nbsp;</font></div><div><font color="#0f172a">4.&nbsp; **Management Durations:** The exact timeline or plan for the Dual Antiplatelet Therapy (DAPT) duration (e.g., 21 days vs. 90 days before transitioning to single antiplatelet therapy) is not documented.</font></div><div></div>